&P365112 = CT 02, pl. 31, Bu 1891-05-09, 260 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. ap-lu-ut ha-li-ia-tum 
#tr.ts: aplūt ḫaliyatum
#tr.en: (Concerning) the inheritance of Ḫaliyatum,
2. sza a-na geme2-{d}utu _dumu-munus_ ia-ku-bi id-di-nu 
#tr.ts: ša ana amat-šamaš mārat iakubi iddinu
#tr.en: that to Amat-šamaš daughter of Iakubi had given,
3. lu!-bu-sza-am pi2-sza-tam 
#tr.ts: lubūšam pi(š)šatam
#tr.en: clothing allowance, oil allotment (and)
4. pi2!-qi2-ta-sza u2-ul id-di-im-ma 
#tr.ts: piqi(t)taša ul iddimma
#tr.en: her provisions (Amat-šamaš) did not provide (her) so
5. _di-ku5-mesz_ i-na e2-babbar2-ri-im 
# blank space at the beginning of the preceding line
#tr.ts: dayyānī ina ebabbarim	
#tr.en: the judges in the Ebabbar
6. {disz}ha-li-ia-tum# 
#tr.ts: ḫaliyatum
#tr.en: Ḫaliyatum
7. u3 geme2-{d}utu isz-szu-da-a-ma
# (Schorr explains iššudama instead of ikšudūma as "Vulgärform"; cp. Schorr VAB 5 p. 355)
#tr.ts: u amat-šamaš ikšudūma
#tr.en: and Amat-šamaš approached and
8. {disz}ha-li-ia-tum 
#tr.ts: ḫaliyatum
#tr.en: Ḫaliyatum
9. {disz}geme2-{d}utu 
#tr.ts: amat-šamaš
#tr.en: Amat-šamaš
10. i-na ap-lu-ti-sza i-su2-uh 
#tr.ts: ina aplūtīša i(s)suḫ
#tr.en: disinherited (lit. removed from her condition of heir).
@reverse 
1. t,up-pu-um sza ha-li-ia-tum 
#tr.ts: ṭuppum ša ḫaliyatum
#tr.en: (When) the tablet, that Ḫaliyatum
2. a-na geme2-{d}utu 
#tr.ts: ana amat-šamaš
#tr.en: to Amat-šamaš
3. ap-lu-sa3 id-di-nu 
#tr.ts: aplu(s)sa iddinu
#tr.en: her heir gave,
4. i-li-a-am sa3-ar i-he-pi2 
#tr.ts: i(l)liam sār i(ḫ)ḫe(p)pi
#tr.en: turns up, it is false (and) shall be destroyed.
5. _mu_ {d}utu {d}a-a {d}amar-utu 
#tr.ts: nīš šamaš aya marduk
#tr.en: By the life of Šamaš, Aya, Marduk
6. u3 sin-mu-ba-li2-it,
#tr.ts: u sîn-muballiṭ
#tr.en: and Sîn-muballiṭ
7. di-in _e2 {d}utu [di]-ku5-mesz_ 
# blank space at the beginning of the preceding line
#tr.ts: dīn bīt šamaš dayyānū
#tr.en: Verdict of (the judges in) the house of Šamaš. The judges:
8. {disz}sin#-i-qi2-sza-am 
#tr.ts: sîn-iqīšam
#tr.en: Sîn-iqīšam;
9. {disz}{d}utu-li-wi-ir! 
#tr.ts: šamaš-li(w)wir
#tr.en: Šamaš-liwwir;
10. {disz}dingir-szu-i-bi-szu 
#tr.ts: ilšu-i(b)bīšu
#tr.en: Ilšu-ibbīšu;
11. {disz}sin-ia-tum 
#tr.ts: sînyatum
#tr.en: Sînyatum;
12. {disz}{d}utu-i3-kusz2 
#tr.ts: utu-ikuš
#tr.en: Utu-ikuš.
